; zerobus-rest-async (§4.2): the Async instantiation of the stateless REST
; insert helper. The Async counterpart of zerobus-rest (Lwt); reuses
; zerobus-core's OAuth body-builder and the SHARED pure-ocaml-tls HTTP backend
; from zerobus-async (Zerobus_async.Oauth.https_post over Tls_async.connect) for
; both the token mint and the insert POST — NOT cohttp-async (whose conduit needs
; OpenSSL). So no OpenSSL dependency, matching the SDK's ocaml-tls posture.
;
; Builds everywhere zerobus-async does; if tls-async is absent at build time the
; shared HTTP backend is the honest-error stub, so insert returns a Transport_error
; rather than performing I/O (same posture as built-in Async OAuth). Not in
; standard CI (a live run needs credentials).
(library
 (name zerobus_rest_async)
 (public_name zerobus-rest-async)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_let))
 (libraries
  zerobus-core
  zerobus-async
  core
  async
  yojson
  base64))
